{"title":"How plants make food from sunlight, water and air","key_idea":"Plants use sunlight to turn water and air into food and oxygen, a process called photosynthesis.","method":["Plants take in water through their roots from the soil.","Plants take in carbon dioxide gas from the air through tiny holes in their leaves called stomata.","Sunlight shines on the green colour (chlorophyll) in the leaves.","The plant uses the energy from sunlight to combine water and carbon dioxide into a sugar called glucose, which is food for the plant.","The plant releases oxygen as a waste product that we breathe."],"worked_example":{"problem":"A potted plant sits on a sunny windowsill with water in the soil. Describe what the plant needs to make food.","steps":["The plant's roots absorb water from the wet soil.","The plant's leaves take in carbon dioxide from the air around it.","Sunlight enters the green leaves from the window.","All three things mix together inside the leaf to make glucose food."],"answer":"The plant uses water from soil, carbon dioxide from air, and sunlight energy to make glucose food."},"key_terms":[{"term":"photosynthesis","meaning":"the process by which plants make their own food using sunlight"},{"term":"chlorophyll","meaning":"the green substance in leaves that catches sunlight"},{"term":"stomata","meaning":"tiny holes in leaves that let air (carbon dioxide) in and out"},{"term":"glucose","meaning":"the sugar food that plants make and use for energy"}],"common_mistakes":["Thinking plants eat food like animals do, instead of making it themselves.","Forgetting that plants need all three things (sunlight, water and air) at the same time."],"remember":"Sunlight + water + air = food + oxygen inside the green leaf.","quick_check":[{"q":"What gas from the air do plants use to make food?","a":"Carbon dioxide."},{"q":"Name two things plants release or produce during photosynthesis.","a":"Glucose (food) and oxygen."}],"tell_your_child":"Plants are like little factories that use the sun's energy to turn water and air into food. Every green leaf you see is busy making food right now if there is sunlight!","picture":{"concept_key":"c5-science-photosynthesis","scene_prompt":"A plant with green leaves sitting in sunlight by a window, with water droplets on the soil and the sun shining brightly."}}
